 2. 🌙 Partial eclipse tonight 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Graphic: NASA Most of the U.S. will be treated to a partial lunar eclipse overnight as the Moon passes into Earth's shadow.

 The result: The Moon will look coppery red, with a thin sliver left partially illuminated. 🌒 The phenomenon peaks just after midnight Eastern Time, when about 96% of the Moon will fall into shadow.

